            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a festive procession, then the Hindi for a devotee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: व्रत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्रत — vrat — \"a fast; a vow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दादी ने पूरे दिन व्रत रखा। dādī ne pūre din vrat rakhā. Grandmother fasted all day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्रत (vrat) is Sanskrit vrata, \"a vow, a rule of conduct\" (Monier-Williams). व्रत रखना is to keep a fast, a vow to go without food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
